<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="h-full">
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) ? "#{content_for(:title)} · Prism" : "Prism" %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
    <%# The browser chrome follows the page. Two tags rather than one, because
        `theme-color` takes no CSS variable and Prism has two canvases — the
        values are `--color-canvas`'s light-dark() pair, so change them
        together with the token. %>
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f2f3f8" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0e1020" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)">
    <meta name="application-name" content="Prism">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>

    <%# Turbo 8 prefetches a link on hover. Prism turns that off everywhere,
        because no screen here is cheap to render: the repository list costs up
        to five GitHub calls, a pull request overview four, the rendered file
        view more again. Prefetching would spend a reviewer's GitHub rate limit
        — a budget PLAN.md already treats as scarce — on every page they merely
        moved the pointer across. Running an eye down a list of twenty pull
        requests would cost twenty page renders.

        This is global rather than per-link on purpose. A per-link opt-out is a
        rule every future link has to remember, and forgetting it fails
        silently as quiet rate-limit burn. If a genuinely cheap screen ever
        exists, opt that link back in with data-turbo-prefetch="true". %>
    <meta name="turbo-prefetch" content="false">

    <%= yield :head %>

    <%# Space Grotesk carries the interface, Source Serif 4 the rendered
        Markdown, JetBrains Mono the code. See DESIGN.md §3. %>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;700&family=Source+Serif+4:ital,opsz,wght@0,8..60,400;0,8..60,600;0,8..60,700;1,8..60,400&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap">

    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.png" type="image/png">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icon.png">

    <%= stylesheet_link_tag :app, "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
  </head>

  <body class="flex min-h-full flex-col bg-canvas text-ink antialiased">
    <%# ── Shell convention ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
        The top bar is rendered here for every signed-in screen; a screen adds
        its own context with `content_for :breadcrumb`. Page content picks one
        width class — `.shell` (browsing), `.reading-shell` (the review
        screen), `.shell-narrow` (sign in) — and never wraps itself in another
        max-width. See DESIGN.md §4. %>
    <% if signed_in? %>
      <%= render "shared/top_bar" %>
    <% end %>

    <%# A stable wrapper so a Turbo Stream can put a message here after a
        write — `_flash` itself renders nothing when there is no flash, so it
        has no id of its own to aim at. ReviewCommentsController#create
        updates this on every comment posted, which also clears a notice left
        over from an earlier one. %>
    <div id="flash"><%= render "shared/flash" %></div>

    <main class="flex-1" id="main">
      <%= yield %>
    </main>

    <%= yield :tray %>
  </body>
</html>
